1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,383
Kaeden:

2
00:00:00,383 --> 00:00:01,209
Hello Charlotte.

3
00:00:01,209 --> 00:00:03,900
I’m Kaeden, one of the supervisors.

4
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:05,460
Welcome to the team.

5
00:00:05,460 --> 00:00:05,977
Charlotte:

6
00:00:05,977 --> 00:00:07,010
Hi Aiden.

7
00:00:07,010 --> 00:00:07,305
Kaeden:

8
00:00:07,305 --> 00:00:08,190
It’s Kaeden.

9
00:00:08,190 --> 00:00:08,526
Charlotte:

10
00:00:08,526 --> 00:00:09,870
I’m so sorry.

11
00:00:09,870 --> 00:00:10,286
Kaeden:

12
00:00:10,286 --> 00:00:11,536
Don’t worry.

13
00:00:11,536 --> 00:00:14,034
People often get my name wrong;

14
00:00:14,034 --> 00:00:16,949
they never know how to spell it.

15
00:00:16,949 --> 00:00:21,530
It’s K-A-E-D-E-N, in case you ever need to write it.

16
00:00:21,530 --> 00:00:21,892
Charlotte:

17
00:00:21,892 --> 00:00:23,700
I’ll try and remember.

18
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:23,989
Kaeden:

19
00:00:23,989 --> 00:00:28,033
So, there are a few practical things you need to sort out this morning.

20
00:00:28,033 --> 00:00:31,500
Then I’ll show you what you’re going to do today.

21
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:31,843
Charlotte:

22
00:00:31,843 --> 00:00:37,675
The email I received said to go to the front desk, to show my letter of appointment

23
00:00:37,675 --> 00:00:39,390
and pick up my badge.

24
00:00:39,390 --> 00:00:39,688
Kaeden:

25
00:00:39,688 --> 00:00:44,156
You’ll need that for the staffroom and other areas of the supermarket where shoppers

26
00:00:44,156 --> 00:00:45,050
aren’t allowed.

27
00:00:45,050 --> 00:00:45,370
Kaeden:

28
00:00:45,370 --> 00:00:50,170
So, after you’ve finished at the front desk, I’ll take you to the

29
00:00:50,170 --> 00:00:50,490
staffroom.

30
00:00:50,490 --> 00:00:54,010
Put your coat and rucksack in one of the lockers there.

31
00:00:54,010 --> 00:00:55,610
Take whichever one is free.

32
00:00:55,610 --> 00:00:55,945
Charlotte:

33
00:00:55,945 --> 00:00:57,620
Will I have a key?

34
00:00:57,620 --> 00:00:57,889
Kaeden:

35
00:00:57,889 --> 00:00:58,158
Yes.

36
00:00:58,158 --> 00:00:59,504
Try not to lose it.

37
00:00:59,504 --> 00:01:03,272
At the end of the day, leave it in the door for the next

38
00:01:03,272 --> 00:01:04,080
person to use.

39
00:01:04,080 --> 00:01:04,510
Charlotte:

40
00:01:04,510 --> 00:01:05,370
Will do.

41
00:01:05,370 --> 00:01:05,672
Kaeden:

42
00:01:05,672 --> 00:01:09,301
You also need to go to the HR department to see Tiffany.

43
00:01:09,301 --> 00:01:10,510
She’s really helpful.

44
00:01:10,510 --> 00:01:10,824
Charlotte:

45
00:01:10,824 --> 00:01:13,653
I was told to bring my passport with me.

46
00:01:13,653 --> 00:01:17,110
HR need to take a note of the number in it.

47
00:01:17,110 --> 00:01:17,360
Kaeden:

48
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:18,110
That’s right.

49
00:01:18,110 --> 00:01:19,860
Or you can show your ID card.

50
00:01:19,860 --> 00:01:20,080
Charlotte:

51
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:21,620
I don’t have one of those.

52
00:01:21,620 --> 00:01:21,962
Kaeden:

53
00:01:21,962 --> 00:01:22,304
OK.

54
00:01:22,304 --> 00:01:24,355
Tiffany will give you a uniform.

55
00:01:24,355 --> 00:01:26,405
They have lots in different sizes,

56
00:01:26,405 --> 00:01:29,140
so you just tell her what you need.

57
00:01:29,140 --> 00:01:29,410
Kaeden:

58
00:01:29,410 --> 00:01:32,914
I won’t come with you to HR – I’ve got to go

59
00:01:32,914 --> 00:01:34,262
and sort something else out.

60
00:01:34,262 --> 00:01:35,610
Problem with a bread slicer.

61
00:01:35,610 --> 00:01:36,031
Charlotte:

62
00:01:36,031 --> 00:01:38,980
Is the HR office near the staffroom?

63
00:01:38,980 --> 00:01:39,275
Kaeden:

64
00:01:39,275 --> 00:01:41,337
The staffroom’s on the first floor,

65
00:01:41,337 --> 00:01:45,167
and HR are a couple of floors above that, on the third floor.

66
00:01:45,167 --> 00:01:47,230
There’s a staircase outside the staffroom.

67
00:01:47,230 --> 00:01:47,870
Charlotte:

68
00:01:47,870 --> 00:01:48,510
OK.

69
00:01:48,510 --> 00:01:48,759
Kaeden:

70
00:01:48,759 --> 00:01:52,492
When you’ve finished with HR, come and find me in the bakery section of

71
00:01:52,492 --> 00:01:52,990
the shop.

72
00:01:52,990 --> 00:01:53,306
Charlotte:

73
00:01:53,306 --> 00:01:55,520
I’m looking forward to getting started.

74
00:01:55,520 --> 00:01:55,780
Kaeden:

75
00:01:55,780 --> 00:01:59,420
I’ll just give you my phone number, in case you can’t find

76
00:01:59,420 --> 00:01:59,680
me.

77
00:01:59,680 --> 00:02:01,240
Have you got your phone there?

78
00:02:01,240 --> 00:02:02,202
Charlotte:

79
00:02:02,202 --> 00:02:03,165
Yes .

80
00:02:03,165 --> 00:02:03,215
.

81
00:02:03,215 --> 00:02:03,265
.

82
00:02:03,265 --> 00:02:05,090
OK, ready.

83
00:02:05,090 --> 00:02:06,333
Kaeden:

84
00:02:06,333 --> 00:02:12,550
It’s oh-four-one-two double-six-five nine-oh-three.

85
00:02:12,550 --> 00:02:13,330
Charlotte:

86
00:02:13,330 --> 00:02:14,890
OK, done.

87
00:02:14,890 --> 00:02:15,317
Kaeden:

88
00:02:15,317 --> 00:02:21,299
So, Charlotte, your tasks today are in the bakery section, on the sushi counter,

89
00:02:21,299 --> 00:02:24,290
and on the meat and fish counters.

90
00:02:24,290 --> 00:02:24,577
Kaeden:

91
00:02:24,577 --> 00:02:28,303
The first job is to check sell-by dates on the bread and cakes.

92
00:02:28,303 --> 00:02:32,603
If any of the dates are today’s, put a new price label on the

93
00:02:32,603 --> 00:02:32,890
packaging.

94
00:02:32,890 --> 00:02:33,274
Charlotte:

95
00:02:33,274 --> 00:02:37,111
What if any of the labels are yesterday’s dates,

96
00:02:37,111 --> 00:02:37,878
or older?

97
00:02:37,878 --> 00:02:40,180
Do I throw those items away?

98
00:02:40,180 --> 00:02:40,470
Kaeden:

99
00:02:40,470 --> 00:02:40,759
Yes,

100
00:02:40,759 --> 00:02:43,946
but that shouldn’t happen – we check the stock every day.

101
00:02:43,946 --> 00:02:48,002
When something needs a new price label, put a yellow one on the package,

102
00:02:48,002 --> 00:02:49,450
next to the original price.

103
00:02:49,450 --> 00:02:50,025
Charlotte:

104
00:02:50,025 --> 00:02:50,600
OK.

105
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:50,954
Kaeden:

106
00:02:50,954 --> 00:02:54,490
After that, you’ll go to the sushi takeaway counter.

107
00:02:54,490 --> 00:02:54,818
Charlotte:

108
00:02:54,818 --> 00:02:57,110
Will I be preparing boxes of food?

109
00:02:57,110 --> 00:02:57,403
Kaeden:

110
00:02:57,403 --> 00:03:00,040
For today, you’ll just be helping the staff.

111
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:00,425
Charlotte:

112
00:03:00,425 --> 00:03:01,580
Yes, of course.

113
00:03:01,580 --> 00:03:01,847
Kaeden:

114
00:03:01,847 --> 00:03:05,590
You’ll see lots of flat cardboard boxes at one end of the counter.

115
00:03:05,590 --> 00:03:05,904
Kaeden:

116
00:03:05,904 --> 00:03:09,986
Beneath those is where we keep the plastic boxes – we run out of

117
00:03:09,986 --> 00:03:10,928
those really quickly,

118
00:03:10,928 --> 00:03:13,440
so you should bring more from the storeroom.

119
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:13,768
Charlotte:

120
00:03:13,768 --> 00:03:16,720
Is that my only task on the sushi counter?

121
00:03:16,720 --> 00:03:17,005
Kaeden:

122
00:03:17,005 --> 00:03:17,290
No.

123
00:03:17,290 --> 00:03:20,712
You also need to clean the area where they prepare the dishes.

124
00:03:20,712 --> 00:03:23,564
There are cloths and bottles of spray by the sink.

125
00:03:23,564 --> 00:03:23,849
Oh,

126
00:03:23,849 --> 00:03:26,130
and please make sure you clean that too.

127
00:03:26,130 --> 00:03:26,466
Charlotte:

128
00:03:26,466 --> 00:03:26,802
Sure.

129
00:03:26,802 --> 00:03:28,820
That’s important, isn’t it?

130
00:03:28,820 --> 00:03:29,117
Kaeden:

131
00:03:29,117 --> 00:03:29,413
Absolutely.

132
00:03:29,413 --> 00:03:31,489
But you mustn’t wash up knives.

133
00:03:31,489 --> 00:03:35,640
You have to do some training before you’re allowed to touch sharp objects.

134
00:03:35,640 --> 00:03:35,923
Charlotte:

135
00:03:35,923 --> 00:03:38,190
What should I do if there are any?

136
00:03:38,190 --> 00:03:38,414
Kaeden:

137
00:03:38,414 --> 00:03:40,210
Ask someone to put them in the dishwasher.

138
00:03:40,210 --> 00:03:40,525
Charlotte:

139
00:03:40,525 --> 00:03:41,154
OK, thanks.

140
00:03:41,154 --> 00:03:43,670
I don’t want to get anything wrong.

141
00:03:43,670 --> 00:03:43,873
Kaeden:

142
00:03:43,873 --> 00:03:44,483
Don’t worry.

143
00:03:44,483 --> 00:03:45,297
You’ll be fine.

144
00:03:45,297 --> 00:03:46,720
And I’ll be around to help.

145
00:03:46,720 --> 00:03:47,235
Charlotte:

146
00:03:47,235 --> 00:03:47,750
Right.

147
00:03:47,750 --> 00:03:48,133
Kaeden:

148
00:03:48,133 --> 00:03:50,432
Finally, the meat and fish counters.

149
00:03:50,432 --> 00:03:55,797
You need to clean the area where staff serve customers, including wiping the weighing

150
00:03:55,797 --> 00:03:56,180
scales.

151
00:03:56,180 --> 00:03:56,955
Charlotte:

152
00:03:56,955 --> 00:03:57,730
OK.

153
00:03:57,730 --> 00:03:59,280
Anything else?

154
00:03:59,280 --> 00:03:59,579
Kaeden:

155
00:03:59,579 --> 00:04:01,374
The fish is laid on ice,

156
00:04:01,374 --> 00:04:05,561
but when that starts to melt, you’ll need to get more from the

157
00:04:05,561 --> 00:04:05,860
cold-room.

158
00:04:05,860 --> 00:04:06,166
Charlotte:

159
00:04:06,166 --> 00:04:09,529
I know the staff on the food counters wear a hat.

160
00:04:09,529 --> 00:04:11,670
Will that be the same for me?

161
00:04:11,670 --> 00:04:11,966
Kaeden:

162
00:04:11,966 --> 00:04:14,038
You won’t be serving customers directly,

163
00:04:14,038 --> 00:04:14,630
so no.

164
00:04:14,630 --> 00:04:14,903
Kaeden:

165
00:04:14,903 --> 00:04:18,725
But make sure you put on thermal gloves when you take anything out of

166
00:04:18,725 --> 00:04:19,271
the cold-room.

167
00:04:19,271 --> 00:04:22,820
The temperature’s low enough in there to get frostbite from touching things.

168
00:04:22,820 --> 00:04:23,885
Charlotte:

169
00:04:23,885 --> 00:04:24,950
Understoood.
